<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Photographs are the most emotionally valuable thing an ordinary family
    owns, and almost every family now rents their custody. The library, the
    sharing, and the cost of leaving all belong to a company, and the bill
    goes up when the storage fills.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is that library, on hardware you own.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What it does</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Takes a folder at a time") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Drag in a decade. Duplicates are skipped, so importing the same
        holiday twice from two phones does what you'd hope rather than what
        you'd fear.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Albums, and who's in them") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Group them however you like, and record who appears — which turns
        "find the ones with dad in" from an afternoon into a search.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Shared deliberately") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        With the household, or outside it by a link that needs no account —
        so the grandmother who will never sign up for anything can still see
        the christening.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "A map, for free") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Photos quietly record where they were taken, so the library also
        draws the map of everywhere you've been — without fetching anything
        from anyone.
        <%= link_to "How that works →", about_feature_path("world-map"), class: "text-primary-700 hover:underline" %>
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Storage, honestly</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Photographs are big, and a family library will outgrow a small disk. The
    app can keep them on your machine or on storage you rent from whoever
    you like, and moving between the two is a setting rather than a
    migration. What it will not do is pretend that ten years of video fits
    anywhere for free.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Back them up somewhere else too. This is the data you would be most
    upset to lose, and self-hosting means the disk that dies is now yours.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What it won't do</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    It will not scan your library to sell you anything, build a face
    database it uses elsewhere, or turn your children into training data.
    The only thing looking at these photographs is the software you're
    running.
  </p>
</section>
